// Content moderation for campaigns and updates (Regulatory & Operational Rules
// §3–4; System Architecture — Moderation Flag entity).
//
// One row per raised concern about a piece of content. A flag comes from one of
// two sources:
//
//   ai     — AI-assisted screening at publication/post time (defamation risk,
//            frivolous claims, sensitive content, accidental third-party PII).
//            `aiGenerated` is true; these are advisory and NEVER auto-reject —
//            they hold content for a human ruling, they do not decide it.
//   report — a member of the public used "report this campaign".
//
// The flag does not itself hide anything; visibility is a property of the target
// (`Case.moderationStatus` / `CaseUpdate.moderationStatus`), which the moderation
// service sets. AI flags hold their target immediately (it must not become
// visible before review); public reports hold only once enough accumulate, so a
// single anonymous report cannot take a live campaign down on its own.
//
// `targetType ∈ {case, update}` (stored as text to avoid enum-keyword pitfalls).
// `caseId` is always the owning case — equal to `targetId` for a case flag, and
// the update's case for an update flag — so the admin queue can group, link, and
// cascade-delete by case.
model ModerationFlag {
  id String @id @default(cuid())

  // What is being flagged. `targetType` is "case" or "update"; `targetId` is that
  // row's id. `caseId` is the owning case for both, for the queue and the FK.
  targetType String
  targetId   String
  case       Case   @relation(fields: [caseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  caseId     String

  // "ai" | "report". `aiGenerated` mirrors source == "ai" and is what the UI reads
  // to label a flag as machine-produced.
  source      String
  aiGenerated Boolean @default(false)

  // "defamation" | "frivolous" | "sensitive" | "pii" for AI flags; "report" for a
  // public report. Free text so the taxonomy can grow without a migration.
  category String
  // The AI's rationale, or the reporter's reason. Shown to the reviewing admin.
  detail   String
  // AI self-reported confidence 0–100; null for public reports.
  confidence Int?

  // "open" until an administrator rules; then "resolved" with a `resolution`.
  status     String  @default("open")
  // "cleared" (content is fine → visible) or "removed" (taken down). Null while open.
  resolution String?
  // The moderator's note on why they kept or removed it. Optional, for the record.
  resolutionNote String?

  // The signed-in account that reported, when there was one. Null for AI flags and
  // for anonymous public reports. A plain id, like the rest of the codebase, so no
  // back-relation is added to the auth `User`.
  reporterId String?

  createdAt    DateTime  @default(now())
  resolvedAt   DateTime?
  resolvedById String?

  @@index([status, createdAt])
  @@index([caseId])
  @@index([targetType, targetId, status])
  @@map("moderation_flag")
}
